{
 "name": "70-heading-unit-header",
 "description": "A currency scale is also a currency header. Its form is the sign with the letters directly before it. £m gives GBP, US$000 and $m give USD by their prefixes in the unit table, and $m alone never gives CAD. HK$ is not in the unit table, so HK$'000 is unknown: it gives no unit, and its $ is never read as a lone $. A heading unit acts only through a unit item (spec 0.10, #315).",
